('h2', "A.3  Latin Maxims and Technical Terms \u2014 Quick Glossary"),
('tbl', (["Term", "Meaning"],
         [["***Primum non nocere***", "'First, do no harm' \u2014 the maxim of **non-maleficence**"],
          ["***Salus aegroti suprema lex***", "'The welfare of the patient is the supreme law' \u2014 **beneficence**"],
          ["***Voluntas aegroti suprema lex***", "'The will of the patient is the supreme law' \u2014 **autonomy**"],
          ["***Res ipsa loquitur***", "'The thing speaks for itself' \u2014 negligence presumed; **burden shifts to the defendant**"],
          ["***Respondeat superior***", "'Let the master answer' \u2014 **vicarious liability**"],
          ["***Qui facit per alium facit per se***", "'He who acts through another acts himself' \u2014 vicarious liability"],
          ["***Volenti non fit injuria***", "'To a willing person no injury is done' \u2014 consent to a known risk as a defence"],
          ["***Novus actus interveniens***", "A new intervening act that breaks the chain of causation"],
          ["***Causa causans***", "The immediate, effective cause of the damage"],
          ["***Uberrima fides***", "'Utmost good faith' \u2014 the governing principle of an insurance contract"],
          ["***In loco parentis***", "'In the place of a parent' \u2014 consent by a person temporarily standing in for a parent"],
          ["***Ethos / Mores / Professio***", "Character / customs / to declare publicly \u2014 roots of *ethics*, *morals*, *profession*"],
          ["**Fiduciary relationship**", "A relationship of trust in which the stronger party must act in the weaker party's interest"],
          ["**Prima facie duty**", "A duty binding unless overridden by a stronger competing duty in the particular case"],
          ["**Paternalism**", "Overriding a person's choices for what one believes to be his own good (hard = over a competent patient; soft = where capacity is impaired)"],
          ["**Therapeutic privilege**", "The narrow exception permitting non-disclosure where disclosure itself would gravely harm the patient"],
          ["**Therapeutic misadventure**", "Injury from treatment given in good faith with due care \u2014 **not** negligence"],
          ["**Medical futility**", "Treatment that cannot achieve its objective or merely prolongs dying \u2014 **no obligation to provide it**"],
          ["**Doctrine of double effect**", "A foreseen but unintended harm may be permissible if the act is good, the intention is good and there is proportionate reason"],
          ["**Privileged communication**", "Lawful disclosure in good faith, to the proper authority, to the extent necessary"],
          ["**Dry labbing**", "Reporting a test that was never performed \u2014 fraud and grave professional misconduct"],
          ["**Delta check**", "Comparison of a result with the same patient's previous result to detect error"],
          ["**Turnaround time (TAT)**", "Interval from test order (or collection) to the result being available and acted upon"],
          ["**Critical / panic value**", "A result so abnormal as to be life-threatening; must be communicated immediately"],
          ["**Read-back**", "The receiver repeating a verbal result or order to confirm accurate transmission"],
          ["**Autoverification**", "Automatic release of results meeting predefined rules, so that staff review only exceptions"],
          ["**Universal / standard precautions**", "Treating **every** specimen as potentially infectious \u2014 protects staff *and* protects confidentiality"],
          ["**Whistle-blowing**", "Reporting unsafe or unethical practice through proper channels"],
          ["**Psychological safety**", "The shared belief that one can speak up, question and admit error without humiliation"],
          ["**Just culture**", "A culture that examines the system rather than punishing the individual, while retaining accountability"],
          ["**Allostatic load**", "The cumulative physiological wear and tear caused by chronic stress"],
          ["**Moral distress**", "The distress of knowing the right course of action but being prevented from taking it"],
          ["**Groupthink**", "Suppression of dissent in a cohesive group, leading to poor decisions"],
          ["**Social loafing**", "Reduced individual effort when working in a group"]],
         [4.6, 12.6],
         "Glossary of maxims and technical terms")),

