('h2', "A.5  Twenty Two-Mark Answers You Should Be Able to Write in Two Lines"),
('n', [
    "**Ethics** \u2014 the systematic study of right and wrong conduct and the standards by which human actions are judged.",
    "**Professionalism** \u2014 the habitual demonstration of competence, character, commitment and accountability in the service of patients.",
    "**Autonomy** \u2014 the competent patient's right to make informed, voluntary decisions about his own body and information.",
    "**Non-maleficence** \u2014 the duty not to inflict harm; *primum non nocere*.",
    "**Beneficence** \u2014 the positive duty to act for the patient's benefit and welfare.",
    "**Justice** \u2014 fairness and non-discrimination in the distribution of benefits, risks and resources.",
    "**Informed consent** \u2014 voluntary agreement by a competent person after adequate disclosure and understanding.",
    "**Confidentiality** \u2014 the duty not to disclose patient information obtained professionally, without consent or lawful justification.",
    "**Privileged communication** \u2014 disclosure made in good faith, to the proper authority, to the extent necessary.",
    "**Critical (panic) value** \u2014 a result so abnormal as to be life-threatening, requiring immediate communication.",
    "**Negligence** \u2014 breach of a duty of care causing damage; requires duty, dereliction, direct causation and damage.",
    "**Res ipsa loquitur** \u2014 'the thing speaks for itself'; negligence is presumed and the burden of proof shifts to the defendant.",
    "**Vicarious liability** \u2014 an employer's liability for his employee's negligence committed in the course of employment.",
    "**Malpractice** \u2014 improper, illegal or negligent professional conduct causing injury to a patient.",
    "**Professional misconduct** \u2014 conduct regarded as disgraceful or dishonourable by professional colleagues of good repute.",
    "**Consumer** \u2014 a person who avails of a service for a consideration paid or promised.",
    "**Deficiency in service** \u2014 any fault, imperfection, shortcoming or inadequacy in the quality or manner of performance of a service.",
    "**Stress** \u2014 the non-specific response of the body to any demand made upon it (Selye).",
    "**Burnout** \u2014 emotional exhaustion, depersonalisation and reduced personal accomplishment from chronic workplace stress.",
    "**Leadership** \u2014 the process of influencing and motivating people towards the achievement of a common goal.",
    "**Team** \u2014 a small group with complementary skills, a common goal and mutual accountability.",
    "**Time management** \u2014 planning, prioritising and controlling one's use of time to achieve goals with least waste and stress.",
    "**Human dignity** \u2014 the inherent, unconditional worth of every person, requiring that he never be treated merely as a means.",
    "**Euthanasia** \u2014 intentional termination of the life of a person with an incurable, painful disease to relieve suffering.",
    "**Brain death** \u2014 irreversible cessation of all functions of the entire brain including the brainstem."
]),

